==Overview==
<tabber>
Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* Good for farming in the [[First Sea]].
* Currently the cheapest fighting style in the game (excluding [[Combat]], which is automatically given for free upon joining).
* All moves have [[AoE]].
* Low [[mastery]] requirements.
*Good combo potential for its price

|'''[Z] Flying Kick'''
* Provides some form of air mobility.

|'''[X] Breakdance'''
* Decent as a combo extender.
* Good for grinding [[Aura]] due to the high amount of individual hits.

|'''[C] Barrage'''
* Decent as a combo extender.
* Good damage.

|'''[V] Overheat'''
* Provides a decent damage boost.
}}

|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* Slowest M1 speed out of all the [[Fighting Styles]], unless the player has an autoclicker ([[Combat]] is slightly faster).
* Although it has good combo potential, its good skills which is X and C, are easily countered by [[Instinct]].
* Pairs badly with [[Buddha]] as the M1 attack is slow and weak, and most of the '''Dark Step''' abilities cannot hit [[Enemies]] while transformed.
* Extremely low damage.
* Outclassed by it's successor, [[Death Step]].
* Long cooldowns.

|'''[Z] Flying Kick'''
* Low damage.
* Small hitbox.
* Can't attack airbone players and NPCs.
* Has a high startup time as the user first needs to aim the move, the flying duration, and endlag.

|'''[X] Breakdance'''
* Lowers the user's hitbox, which could be problematic, especially when paired with [[Buddha]], as it removes the invulnerability against some moves. (examples: [[Mythological Pirate]]s' [[Electric]] X) It can also drown the user if they are too close to the sea surface.
* Locks the user in place and can be punished easily due to high endlag.
* Small hitbox.

|'''[C] Barrage'''
* Has to be held for full damage.
* Low range.

|'''[V] Overheat'''
* Can leave the user very vulnerable since it has a long animation.
* Extremely long cooldown compared to buff duration  (1 minute and 30 second cooldown, versus 60 second buff).
}}

|-|Notes=
{{Overview|Notes|
* Dark Step is a good [[Fighting Styles|Fighting Style]] for beginners. Dark Step could theoretically also be good even until late game, since it has very high damage with '''[V] Overheat''' activated. It doesn't have much knockback either, so it can be good for grinding.
** However, it is suggested to first purchase [[Water Kung Fu]] or [[Electric]] instead because of the more varied moves, higher damage and better M1s.
* It is recommended to grind mastery on Dark Step last when trying to get [[Superhuman]], because it does low damage and is generally more difficult than the others.
* When grinding with [[Buddha]], it is recommended to spam [M1] attacks rather than use the moves of Dark Step, as most of them do not work or have extremely unusual/warped hitboxes.
* Dark Step with [[Stun]] Fruits like [[Ice]] can be used for PvP, but only its stun moves that can be used as combo extenders such as '''[C] Barrage''' or '''[X] Breakdance''' are [[Instinct]] dodged, so to [[Break Instinct]], you must use [[Cyborg]] V3 when you start to use '''[X]''' and '''[C]''' on your combos.}}
</tabber>

